            <div xml:id="d188">

                <pb facs="0164" n="156" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg156"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.94/175: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Matthews</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vichy</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-27T19:00:00+02:00">September 27, 1940—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>651. Chauvel tells me the situation in Indochina has greatly improved; word has
                    just been received from Hanoi that Japanese advance posts in the Langson area
                    have begun to withdraw; that some 2,000 troops which debarked at Dosan are to be
                    considered as part of the 6,000 agreed upon and that the commander of the Canton
                    army is being removed.</p>
                <p>He said in strict confidence that this “improvement” had required intervention
                    from the highest quarter, namely the Emperor, to bring it about.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Matthews</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
